       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify that a protocol exists, and I don't know of any amlodipine protocol that uses 50 mg once daily. That dose is far above the labeled maximum of 10 mg. An overdose can cause profound hypotension and shock that can last for days. If the order is wrong, the harm could be severe and hard to reverse.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range**, such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily. I can do that now.\n- **Use your hospital's high-dose override pathway.** This is usually a prescriber entry with pharmacist verification, so the protocol is documented in the system and not only in my note.\n- **Give me the protocol name or document reference**, and I'll put it in the order note. I still can't confirm it myself, so I'd want the dose checked by the pharmacist.\n\nTell me which you'd like and I'll proceed."
      }
